event: content_block_delta
data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/dev_dispatch1.md\", \"content\": \"This is your first real work dispatch (mission: \\\"greet, tested\\\").\\n\\nImplement exactly the following in the subject repository, on your own branch:\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` — a function `greet(name)` that returns the string\\n   `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` (i.e. `greet(\\\"World\\\")` returns `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`).\\n\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` — unit tests (using the standard `unittest` module)\\n   that cover:\\n   - a normal name, e.g. `greet(\\\"World\\\")` == `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`\\n   - the empty string, e.g. `greet(\\\"\\\")` == `\\\"Hello, !\\\"`\\n\\n3. Verify the tests pass by running, from the repo root:\\n   `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`\\n   This must exit 0.\\n\\nDo not add anything beyond this scope (no README updates, no packaging, no\\nextra features). Commit your work to your own branch before replying.\\n\\nIn your reply, report:\\n- the exact command you ran to verify tests, and its exit code / output\\n- confirmation that you committed the changes (include the commit hash)\\n- the contents of src/greet.py and tests/test_greet.py (or state that they\\n  are unchanged from a prior attempt, if this is a rework)\\n\\nTell the truth — if something didn't work, say so rather than reporting\\nsuccess.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

